{"id": "ch-09", "number": 9, "roman": "IX", "title": "Ablative Case, Prepositions, Eō", "blocks": [{"t": "h", "text": "9.1 Ablative"}, {"t": "p", "text": "The last case is the ablative. In the declensions we have so far seen, the ablative endings are the same as those of the dative except in the singular of the first declension and in the feminine singular of adjectives: in those forms it ends in a long -ā. The length of the -ā is important because it serves to distinguish the ablative from the nominative. With the ablative added, the paradigms we have seen can be completed; words ending in -r and in -ius have the same ablative forms as other second-declension words, so the paradigms seen in chapter 8 pose no additional difficulties."}, {"t": "p", "text": "British Case Order"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -a, -us, and –um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "First declension Singular", "Plural", "Second declension masculine Singular Plural", "", "Second declension neuter Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puella", "puellae", "servus", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Voc.", "puella", "puellae", "serve", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Acc.", "puellam", "puellās", "servum", "servōs", "bellum", "bella"], ["Gen.", "puellae", "puellārum", "servī", "servōrum", "bellī", "bellōrum"], ["Dat.", "puellae", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Abl.", "puellā", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in -us, -a, -um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "bonus", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Voc.", "bone", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Acc.", "bonum", "bonam", "bonum", "bonōs", "bonās", "bona"], ["Gen.", "bonī", "bonae", "bonī", "bonōrum", "bonārum", "bonōrum"], ["Dat.", "bonō", "bonae", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Abl.", "bonō", "bonā", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "British Case Order (continued)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -r and –ius"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular", "Plural", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puer", "puerī", "magister  magistrī", "", "vir", "virī", "fīlius", "fīliī"], ["Voc.", "puer", "puerī", "magister  magistrī", "", "vir", "virī", "fīlī", "fīliī"], ["Acc.", "puerum", "puerōs", "magistrum magistrōs", "", "virum", "virōs", "fīlium", "fīliōs"], ["Gen.", "puerī", "puerōrum magistrī  magistrōrum virī", "", "", "", "virōrum", "fīlī/fīliī", "fīliōrum"], ["Dat.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō magistrīs", "", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Abl.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō magistrīs", "", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in –r"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Voc.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Acc.", "nigrum", "nigram", "nigrum", "nigrōs", "nigrās", "nigra"], ["Gen.", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigrī", "nigrōrum", "nigrārum", "nigrōrum"], ["Dat.", "nigrō", "nigrae", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["Abl.", "nigrō", "nigrā", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["", "Singular", "", "", "Plural", "", ""], ["", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], ["Nom.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Voc.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Acc.", "tenerum", "teneram", "tenerum", "tenerōs", "tenerās", "tenera"], ["Gen.", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenerī", "tenerōrum", "tenerārum", "tenerōrum"], ["Dat.", "tenerō", "tenerae", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"], ["Abl.", "tenerō", "tenerā", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Ancient1 Case Order"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -a, -us, and –um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "First declension Singular Plural", "", "Second declension masculine Singular Plural", "", "Second declension neuter Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puella", "puellae", "servus", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Gen.", "puellae", "puellārum", "servī", "servōrum", "bellī", "bellōrum"], ["Dat.", "puellae", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Acc.", "puellam", "puellās", "servum", "servōs", "bellum", "bella"], ["Abl.", "puellā", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Voc.", "puella", "puellae", "serve", "servī", "bellum", "bella"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in -us, -a, -um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "bonus", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Gen.", "bonī", "bonae", "bonī", "bonōrum", "bonārum", "bonōrum"], ["Dat.", "bonō", "bonae", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Acc.", "bonum", "bonam", "bonum", "bonōs", "bonās", "bona"], ["Abl.", "bonō", "bonā", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Voc.", "bone", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -r and –ius"}, {"t": "note", "n": 1, "text": "Strictly speaking, this is a slightly modified version of the ancient order: the actual ancient order was nominative, genitive, dative, accusative, vocative, ablative, but now the vocative is usually positioned after the ablative by adherents of this case order. Many words either have no vocative at all or have no vocative separate from the nominative; with this case order the vocative line is usually omitted in such forms. When using the British order, however, it is unsafe to leave out the vocative line as doing so can lead to uncertainty about which case labels attach to which lines of a paradigm that one has memorized."}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular", "Plural", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puer", "puerī", "magister", "magistrī", "vir", "virī", "fīlius", "fīliī"], ["Gen.", "puerī", "puerōrum magistrī", "", "magistrōrum", "virī", "virōrum fīlī/fīliī", "", "fīliōrum"], ["Dat.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō", "magistrīs", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Acc.", "puerum", "puerōs", "magistrum", "magistrōs", "virum", "virōs", "fīlium", "fīliōs"], ["Abl.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō", "magistrīs", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Voc.", "puer", "puerī", "magister", "magistrī", "vir", "virī", "fīlī", "fīliī"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in –r"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine Feminine Neuter", "", "", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom./Voc.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Gen.", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigrī", "nigrōrum", "nigrārum", "nigrōrum"], ["Dat.", "nigrō", "nigrae", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["Acc.", "nigrum", "nigram", "nigrum", "nigrōs", "nigrās", "nigra"], ["Abl.", "nigrō", "nigrā", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["", "Singular", "", "", "Plural", "", ""], ["", "Masculine Feminine Neuter", "", "", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], ["Nom./Voc.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Gen.", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenerī", "tenerōrum", "tenerārum", "tenerōrum"], ["Dat.", "tenerō", "tenerae", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"], ["Acc.", "tenerum", "teneram", "tenerum", "tenerōs", "tenerās", "tenera"], ["Abl.", "tenerō", "tenerā", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"]]}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "A", "text": "Decline in all six cases of the forms indicated:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "poēta, singular", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "līber ‘free’, neuter plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "meus, masculine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "liber ‘book’, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "pulcher, feminine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "oppidum, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "ager, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "miser, feminine singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "vester, feminine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "asper, neuter singular"}, {"t": "h", "text": "9.2 Prepositions"}, {"t": "p", "text": "The ablative is used in a variety of ways, including after many prepositions."}, {"t": "p", "text": "Prepositions in Latin always govern a particular case or cases; for example cum, which means ‘with’ (in the sense of accompaniment, as ‘John came with Mark’), is always followed by a word in the ablative, whereas ad ‘to’ (in the sense of motion towards, as ‘we went to the beach’) is always followed by a word in the accusative. Some of the most important prepositions and the cases they take are the following:"}, {"t": "p", "text": "ā, ab + ablative ‘from’, ‘away from’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "cum + ablative ‘with’ (accompaniment)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "dē + ablative ‘from’, ‘about’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "ē, ex + ablative ‘out of’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "sine + ablative ‘without’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "in + ablative ‘in’, ‘on’ (without motion towards, as ‘He was swimming in the water’) in + accusative ‘into’, ‘onto’ (with motion towards, as ‘He dived into the water’) ad + accusative ‘to’ (with motion towards)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "per + accusative ‘through’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "trāns + accusative ‘across’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "The basic principle is that motion towards takes the accusative, motion from takes the ablative, and lack of motion also takes the ablative. Nevertheless, some prepositions always take the same case regardless of the particular context in which they occur."}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "B", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "nostri in castris nunc sunt.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "filius tuus cum pueris est."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "boni epistulas scriptas ad servos non mittunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "equos trans agros heri duxerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "nostros in castra duxit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "servum ad oppidum vestrum cras mittet."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "pulchrae per castros currere non possunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "sine consilio tuo vincere non possumus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "filios nostros per castra duxit poeta laudatus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "servus meus ex oppido cucurrit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "miseros iuvare possumus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "Luci, scribesne librum de bello?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "Romani pulchras amaverunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "servus tuus a castris cucurrit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "agricolae in agro stant."}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "dei Romanos in bellum miserunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "sine deo regere paene non potuerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "nostri Graecos sine bello vicerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "servos vestros ad castra hodie mittent."}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "magister pueros trans oppidum hodie duxit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 21, "text": "per silvam equos ad aquam ducemus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 22, "text": "Graeci epistulas scriptas ad Romanos miserunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 23, "text": "nunc equi e silva currunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 24, "text": "legesne librum meum de equis?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 25, "text": "pueri ab agricola magno cucurrerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 26, "text": "ubi sunt pueri? cum magistro nunc stant."}, {"t": "li", "n": 27, "text": "Graeci per agros cucurrerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 28, "text": "sine gladio vincere non potuit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 29, "text": "equi in silva non sunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 30, "text": "equos in silvam ducent agricolae."}, {"t": "li", "n": 31, "text": "verba tua de silvis in libro meo scripsi."}, {"t": "li", "n": 32, "text": "cum servis a castris cucurrimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 33, "text": "sine servis e castris cucurrimus."}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "C", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "Son, will you lead the horses through rough stones?", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "I wrote a book about wars."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "Where is my son? Here, with the learned poets."}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "Is your son in the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "Did you lead our men into the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "Without money I am miserable."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "The boys ran away from the teacher yesterday."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "The Greeks ran out of the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "I shall not lead my horse across the field."}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "The boys ran to the good teacher."}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "The Romans ran through the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "The Greeks conquered our men in the town."}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "The miserable men are standing with the poet."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "Son, did you lead the Greeks to our town?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "The beautiful women sent slaves to the camp of the Romans."}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "Our men saw Greeks in the fields."}, {"t": "h", "text": "9.3 Eō"}, {"t": "p", "text": "The Latin verb ‘go’, like ‘be’ and ‘can’, is irregular. It is eō, īre, iī/īvī, itum, conjugated as follows:"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["Present active indicative", "", "Future active indicative", "", "Perfect active indicative", ""], "rows": [["eō", "‘I go’, ‘I am going’", "ībō", "‘I will go’,", "iī, īvī", "‘I went’, ‘I have"], ["", "", "", "‘I shall go’", "", "gone’"], ["īs", "‘you (singular) go’,", "ībis", "‘you (singular)", "īstī, īvistī", "‘you (singular)"], ["", "‘you (singular) are", "", "will go’, ‘you", "", "went’, you"], ["", "going’", "", "(singular) shall", "", "(singular) have gone’"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", ""], ["it", "‘he/she/it goes’,", "ībit", "‘he/she/it will", "iit, īvit", "‘he/she/it went’,"], ["", "‘he/she/it is", "", "go’, ‘he/she/it", "", "‘he/she/it has"], ["", "going’, ‘goes’, ‘is", "", "shall go’, ‘will", "", "gone’, ‘went’,"], ["", "going’", "", "go’, ‘shall go’", "", "‘has gone’"], ["īmus", "‘we go’, ‘we are", "ībimus", "‘we will go’,", "iimus, īvimus", "‘we went’, ‘we"], ["", "going’", "", "‘we shall go’", "", "have gone’"], ["ītis", "‘you (plural) go’,", "ībitis", "‘you (plural)", "īstis, īvistis", "‘you (plural)"], ["", "‘you (plural) are", "", "will go’, ‘you", "", "went’, ‘you"], ["", "going’", "", "(plural) shall", "", "(plural) have"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", "gone’"], ["eunt", "‘they go’, ‘they are", "ībunt", "‘they will go’,", "iērunt,", "‘they went’, ‘they"], ["", "going’, ‘go’, ‘are", "", "‘they shall go’,", "īvērunt", "have gone’,"], ["", "going’", "", "‘will go’, ‘shall", "", "‘went’, ‘have"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", "gone’"]]}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "D", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "ibimus", "cols": 3}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "iit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "is"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "ibit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "ivisti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "eunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "ibitis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "iimus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "it"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "ibis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "ii"}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "ibunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "istis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "imus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "isti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "ivi"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "ivimus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "eo"}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "ibo"}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "itis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 21, "text": "ivisti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 22, "text": "ivit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 23, "text": "ierunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 24, "text": "iverunt"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "E", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "they will go", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "he will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "she is going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "they go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "it has gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "they went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "I am going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "we shall go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "we are going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "we have gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "I went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "I shall go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "you (singular) go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "you (plural) will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "you (plural) went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "you (singular) went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "you (plural) go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "you (singular) will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "they have gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "he goes"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "F", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "agricolae ad agros ierunt.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "agricola trans agros iit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "agricolae, ivistisne per agros?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "agricola, istine ex agro?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "ab agris ivimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "in agrum ii."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "puer in silvam ibit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "pueri ad silvas ibunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "puer, ibisne e silva?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "pueri, ibitisne trans silvas?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "per silvas ibo."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "a silva ibimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "puellae in aquam eunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "puella ad aquam it."}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "puellae, itisne trans aquam?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "puella, isne per aquam?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "ab aqua imus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "ex aqua eo."}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "G", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "I shall go to the town tomorrow.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "We are going away from the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "Are you (singular) going into the water?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "Did you (plural) go out of the town?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "Boys do not go into war."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "The horses went across the forest."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "I went away from the town."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "We went through the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "Will you (singular) go into the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "The miserable girl is going to the rock."}, {"t": "h", "text": "9.4 Vocabulary to Learn"}, {"t": "vhead", "text": "Verb"}, {"t": "table", "header": null, "rows": [["eō, īre, iī/īvī, itum", "‘go’"], ["ā, ab (+ ablative)", "‘from’, ‘away from’"], ["ad (+ accusative)", "‘to’"], ["cum (+ ablative)", "‘with’"], ["dē (+ ablative)", "‘from’, ‘about’"], ["ē, ex (+ ablative)", "‘out of’"], ["in (+ ablative)", "‘in’, ‘on’"], ["in (+ accusative)", "‘into’, ‘onto’"], ["per (+ accusative)", "‘through’"], ["sine (+ ablative)", "‘without’"], ["trāns (+ accusative)", "‘across’"]]}], "sections": [{"id": "section-1", "latin": "9.1 Ablative", "num": "9.1", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "The last case is the ablative. In the declensions we have so far seen, the ablative endings are the same as those of the dative except in the singular of the first declension and in the feminine singular of adjectives: in those forms it ends in a long -ā. The length of the -ā is important because it serves to distinguish the ablative from the nominative. With the ablative added, the paradigms we have seen can be completed; words ending in -r and in -ius have the same ablative forms as other second-declension words, so the paradigms seen in chapter 8 pose no additional difficulties."}, {"t": "p", "text": "British Case Order"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -a, -us, and –um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "First declension Singular", "Plural", "Second declension masculine Singular Plural", "", "Second declension neuter Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puella", "puellae", "servus", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Voc.", "puella", "puellae", "serve", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Acc.", "puellam", "puellās", "servum", "servōs", "bellum", "bella"], ["Gen.", "puellae", "puellārum", "servī", "servōrum", "bellī", "bellōrum"], ["Dat.", "puellae", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Abl.", "puellā", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in -us, -a, -um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "bonus", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Voc.", "bone", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Acc.", "bonum", "bonam", "bonum", "bonōs", "bonās", "bona"], ["Gen.", "bonī", "bonae", "bonī", "bonōrum", "bonārum", "bonōrum"], ["Dat.", "bonō", "bonae", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Abl.", "bonō", "bonā", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "British Case Order (continued)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -r and –ius"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular", "Plural", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puer", "puerī", "magister  magistrī", "", "vir", "virī", "fīlius", "fīliī"], ["Voc.", "puer", "puerī", "magister  magistrī", "", "vir", "virī", "fīlī", "fīliī"], ["Acc.", "puerum", "puerōs", "magistrum magistrōs", "", "virum", "virōs", "fīlium", "fīliōs"], ["Gen.", "puerī", "puerōrum magistrī  magistrōrum virī", "", "", "", "virōrum", "fīlī/fīliī", "fīliōrum"], ["Dat.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō magistrīs", "", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Abl.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō magistrīs", "", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in –r"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Voc.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Acc.", "nigrum", "nigram", "nigrum", "nigrōs", "nigrās", "nigra"], ["Gen.", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigrī", "nigrōrum", "nigrārum", "nigrōrum"], ["Dat.", "nigrō", "nigrae", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["Abl.", "nigrō", "nigrā", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["", "Singular", "", "", "Plural", "", ""], ["", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], ["Nom.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Voc.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Acc.", "tenerum", "teneram", "tenerum", "tenerōs", "tenerās", "tenera"], ["Gen.", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenerī", "tenerōrum", "tenerārum", "tenerōrum"], ["Dat.", "tenerō", "tenerae", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"], ["Abl.", "tenerō", "tenerā", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Ancient1 Case Order"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -a, -us, and –um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "First declension Singular Plural", "", "Second declension masculine Singular Plural", "", "Second declension neuter Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puella", "puellae", "servus", "servī", "bellum", "bella"], ["Gen.", "puellae", "puellārum", "servī", "servōrum", "bellī", "bellōrum"], ["Dat.", "puellae", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Acc.", "puellam", "puellās", "servum", "servōs", "bellum", "bella"], ["Abl.", "puellā", "puellīs", "servō", "servīs", "bellō", "bellīs"], ["Voc.", "puella", "puellae", "serve", "servī", "bellum", "bella"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in -us, -a, -um"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom.", "bonus", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"], ["Gen.", "bonī", "bonae", "bonī", "bonōrum", "bonārum", "bonōrum"], ["Dat.", "bonō", "bonae", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Acc.", "bonum", "bonam", "bonum", "bonōs", "bonās", "bona"], ["Abl.", "bonō", "bonā", "bonō", "bonīs", "bonīs", "bonīs"], ["Voc.", "bone", "bona", "bonum", "bonī", "bonae", "bona"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Nouns in -r and –ius"}, {"t": "note", "n": 1, "text": "Strictly speaking, this is a slightly modified version of the ancient order: the actual ancient order was nominative, genitive, dative, accusative, vocative, ablative, but now the vocative is usually positioned after the ablative by adherents of this case order. Many words either have no vocative at all or have no vocative separate from the nominative; with this case order the vocative line is usually omitted in such forms. When using the British order, however, it is unsafe to leave out the vocative line as doing so can lead to uncertainty about which case labels attach to which lines of a paradigm that one has memorized."}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular", "Plural", "Singular Plural", "", "Singular Plural", ""], "rows": [["Nom.", "puer", "puerī", "magister", "magistrī", "vir", "virī", "fīlius", "fīliī"], ["Gen.", "puerī", "puerōrum magistrī", "", "magistrōrum", "virī", "virōrum fīlī/fīliī", "", "fīliōrum"], ["Dat.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō", "magistrīs", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Acc.", "puerum", "puerōs", "magistrum", "magistrōs", "virum", "virōs", "fīlium", "fīliōs"], ["Abl.", "puerō", "puerīs", "magistrō", "magistrīs", "virō", "virīs", "fīliō", "fīliīs"], ["Voc.", "puer", "puerī", "magister", "magistrī", "vir", "virī", "fīlī", "fīliī"]]}, {"t": "p", "text": "Adjectives in –r"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["", "Singular Masculine Feminine Neuter", "", "", "Plural Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], "rows": [["Nom./Voc.", "niger", "nigra", "nigrum", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigra"], ["Gen.", "nigrī", "nigrae", "nigrī", "nigrōrum", "nigrārum", "nigrōrum"], ["Dat.", "nigrō", "nigrae", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["Acc.", "nigrum", "nigram", "nigrum", "nigrōs", "nigrās", "nigra"], ["Abl.", "nigrō", "nigrā", "nigrō", "nigrīs", "nigrīs", "nigrīs"], ["", "Singular", "", "", "Plural", "", ""], ["", "Masculine Feminine Neuter", "", "", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter"], ["Nom./Voc.", "tener", "tenera", "tenerum", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenera"], ["Gen.", "tenerī", "tenerae", "tenerī", "tenerōrum", "tenerārum", "tenerōrum"], ["Dat.", "tenerō", "tenerae", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"], ["Acc.", "tenerum", "teneram", "tenerum", "tenerōs", "tenerās", "tenera"], ["Abl.", "tenerō", "tenerā", "tenerō", "tenerīs", "tenerīs", "tenerīs"]]}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "A", "text": "Decline in all six cases of the forms indicated:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "poēta, singular", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "līber ‘free’, neuter plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "meus, masculine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "liber ‘book’, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "pulcher, feminine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "oppidum, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "ager, singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "miser, feminine singular"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "vester, feminine plural"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "asper, neuter singular"}]}, {"id": "section-2", "latin": "9.2 Prepositions", "num": "9.2", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "The ablative is used in a variety of ways, including after many prepositions."}, {"t": "p", "text": "Prepositions in Latin always govern a particular case or cases; for example cum, which means ‘with’ (in the sense of accompaniment, as ‘John came with Mark’), is always followed by a word in the ablative, whereas ad ‘to’ (in the sense of motion towards, as ‘we went to the beach’) is always followed by a word in the accusative. Some of the most important prepositions and the cases they take are the following:"}, {"t": "p", "text": "ā, ab + ablative ‘from’, ‘away from’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "cum + ablative ‘with’ (accompaniment)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "dē + ablative ‘from’, ‘about’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "ē, ex + ablative ‘out of’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "sine + ablative ‘without’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "in + ablative ‘in’, ‘on’ (without motion towards, as ‘He was swimming in the water’) in + accusative ‘into’, ‘onto’ (with motion towards, as ‘He dived into the water’) ad + accusative ‘to’ (with motion towards)"}, {"t": "p", "text": "per + accusative ‘through’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "trāns + accusative ‘across’"}, {"t": "p", "text": "The basic principle is that motion towards takes the accusative, motion from takes the ablative, and lack of motion also takes the ablative. Nevertheless, some prepositions always take the same case regardless of the particular context in which they occur."}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "B", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "nostri in castris nunc sunt.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "filius tuus cum pueris est."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "boni epistulas scriptas ad servos non mittunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "equos trans agros heri duxerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "nostros in castra duxit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "servum ad oppidum vestrum cras mittet."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "pulchrae per castros currere non possunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "sine consilio tuo vincere non possumus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "filios nostros per castra duxit poeta laudatus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "servus meus ex oppido cucurrit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "miseros iuvare possumus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "Luci, scribesne librum de bello?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "Romani pulchras amaverunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "servus tuus a castris cucurrit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "agricolae in agro stant."}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "dei Romanos in bellum miserunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "sine deo regere paene non potuerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "nostri Graecos sine bello vicerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "servos vestros ad castra hodie mittent."}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "magister pueros trans oppidum hodie duxit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 21, "text": "per silvam equos ad aquam ducemus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 22, "text": "Graeci epistulas scriptas ad Romanos miserunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 23, "text": "nunc equi e silva currunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 24, "text": "legesne librum meum de equis?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 25, "text": "pueri ab agricola magno cucurrerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 26, "text": "ubi sunt pueri? cum magistro nunc stant."}, {"t": "li", "n": 27, "text": "Graeci per agros cucurrerunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 28, "text": "sine gladio vincere non potuit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 29, "text": "equi in silva non sunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 30, "text": "equos in silvam ducent agricolae."}, {"t": "li", "n": 31, "text": "verba tua de silvis in libro meo scripsi."}, {"t": "li", "n": 32, "text": "cum servis a castris cucurrimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 33, "text": "sine servis e castris cucurrimus."}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "C", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "Son, will you lead the horses through rough stones?", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "I wrote a book about wars."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "Where is my son? Here, with the learned poets."}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "Is your son in the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "Did you lead our men into the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "Without money I am miserable."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "The boys ran away from the teacher yesterday."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "The Greeks ran out of the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "I shall not lead my horse across the field."}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "The boys ran to the good teacher."}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "The Romans ran through the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "The Greeks conquered our men in the town."}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "The miserable men are standing with the poet."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "Son, did you lead the Greeks to our town?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "The beautiful women sent slaves to the camp of the Romans."}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "Our men saw Greeks in the fields."}]}, {"id": "section-3", "latin": "9.3 Eō", "num": "9.3", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "The Latin verb ‘go’, like ‘be’ and ‘can’, is irregular. It is eō, īre, iī/īvī, itum, conjugated as follows:"}, {"t": "table", "header": ["Present active indicative", "", "Future active indicative", "", "Perfect active indicative", ""], "rows": [["eō", "‘I go’, ‘I am going’", "ībō", "‘I will go’,", "iī, īvī", "‘I went’, ‘I have"], ["", "", "", "‘I shall go’", "", "gone’"], ["īs", "‘you (singular) go’,", "ībis", "‘you (singular)", "īstī, īvistī", "‘you (singular)"], ["", "‘you (singular) are", "", "will go’, ‘you", "", "went’, you"], ["", "going’", "", "(singular) shall", "", "(singular) have gone’"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", ""], ["it", "‘he/she/it goes’,", "ībit", "‘he/she/it will", "iit, īvit", "‘he/she/it went’,"], ["", "‘he/she/it is", "", "go’, ‘he/she/it", "", "‘he/she/it has"], ["", "going’, ‘goes’, ‘is", "", "shall go’, ‘will", "", "gone’, ‘went’,"], ["", "going’", "", "go’, ‘shall go’", "", "‘has gone’"], ["īmus", "‘we go’, ‘we are", "ībimus", "‘we will go’,", "iimus, īvimus", "‘we went’, ‘we"], ["", "going’", "", "‘we shall go’", "", "have gone’"], ["ītis", "‘you (plural) go’,", "ībitis", "‘you (plural)", "īstis, īvistis", "‘you (plural)"], ["", "‘you (plural) are", "", "will go’, ‘you", "", "went’, ‘you"], ["", "going’", "", "(plural) shall", "", "(plural) have"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", "gone’"], ["eunt", "‘they go’, ‘they are", "ībunt", "‘they will go’,", "iērunt,", "‘they went’, ‘they"], ["", "going’, ‘go’, ‘are", "", "‘they shall go’,", "īvērunt", "have gone’,"], ["", "going’", "", "‘will go’, ‘shall", "", "‘went’, ‘have"], ["", "", "", "go’", "", "gone’"]]}, {"t": "practice"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "D", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "ibimus", "cols": 3}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "iit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "is"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "ibit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "ivisti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "eunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "ibitis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "iimus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "it"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "ibis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "ii"}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "ibunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "istis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "imus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "isti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "ivi"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "ivimus"}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "eo"}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "ibo"}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "itis"}, {"t": "li", "n": 21, "text": "ivisti"}, {"t": "li", "n": 22, "text": "ivit"}, {"t": "li", "n": 23, "text": "ierunt"}, {"t": "li", "n": 24, "text": "iverunt"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "E", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "they will go", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "he will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "she is going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "they go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "it has gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "they went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "I am going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "we shall go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "we are going"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "we have gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "I went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "I shall go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "you (singular) go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "you (plural) will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "you (plural) went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "you (singular) went"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "you (plural) go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "you (singular) will go"}, {"t": "li", "n": 19, "text": "they have gone"}, {"t": "li", "n": 20, "text": "he goes"}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "F", "text": "Translate:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "agricolae ad agros ierunt.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "agricola trans agros iit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "agricolae, ivistisne per agros?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "agricola, istine ex agro?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "ab agris ivimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "in agrum ii."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "puer in silvam ibit."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "pueri ad silvas ibunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "puer, ibisne e silva?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "pueri, ibitisne trans silvas?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 11, "text": "per silvas ibo."}, {"t": "li", "n": 12, "text": "a silva ibimus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 13, "text": "puellae in aquam eunt."}, {"t": "li", "n": 14, "text": "puella ad aquam it."}, {"t": "li", "n": 15, "text": "puellae, itisne trans aquam?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 16, "text": "puella, isne per aquam?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 17, "text": "ab aqua imus."}, {"t": "li", "n": 18, "text": "ex aqua eo."}, {"t": "ex", "letter": "G", "text": "Translate into Latin:"}, {"t": "li", "n": 1, "text": "I shall go to the town tomorrow.", "cols": 2}, {"t": "li", "n": 2, "text": "We are going away from the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 3, "text": "Are you (singular) going into the water?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 4, "text": "Did you (plural) go out of the town?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 5, "text": "Boys do not go into war."}, {"t": "li", "n": 6, "text": "The horses went across the forest."}, {"t": "li", "n": 7, "text": "I went away from the town."}, {"t": "li", "n": 8, "text": "We went through the camp."}, {"t": "li", "n": 9, "text": "Will you (singular) go into the camp?"}, {"t": "li", "n": 10, "text": "The miserable girl is going to the rock."}]}, {"id": "section-4", "latin": "9.4 Vocabulary to Learn", "num": "9.4", "blocks": [{"t": "vhead", "text": "Verb"}, {"t": "table", "header": null, "rows": [["eō, īre, iī/īvī, itum", "‘go’"], ["ā, ab (+ ablat